Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     T43852 "IPv4_DHCPServer - DHCP Relay". No step text exists for this case in
          AWPTCM or ck.db, so it was graded against:
            - X960 platform support TPS, row 28: DHCP Relay, priority 1, Yes;
            - DHCP Feature Overview and Configuration Guide C613-22102-00 REV G;
            - AW+ CLI pages service-dhcp-relay (enabled by default),
              ip-dhcp-relay-server-address (interface mode),
              ip-dhcp-relay-maxhops (<1-255>, default 10).
          4 steps as executed, plus a baseline.
Build:    swi_d  sin_x96056-20261012-24  (flash:/x960-tb277.rel, build date Mon Oct 12 2026)
          AT-x960-56YSQ, S/N A2WQS700B, standalone Active Master, console u2 @115200
Configs:  swi_d.cfg (running-config after setup; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- the DUT relays DHCP in both directions, rewriting giaddr to the
client-side SVI and incrementing hops; both negative controls relayed exactly zero on
identical cabling and traffic, and the hop-count threshold is enforced at its
documented default of 10.
      client frames relayed to the server .... 10 of 10   (5 DISCOVER + 5 REQUEST, eth4 capture)
      giaddr rewritten ...................... 0.0.0.0 -> 192.168.10.1   (all 5 clients)
      hops incremented ...................... 0 -> 1              (all 5 clients)
      relayed source / destination .......... 192.168.48.1 -> 192.168.48.2, unicast
      client chaddr preserved ............... 5 distinct chaddrs, 5 distinct leases
      replies delivered back to the client .. offers 5/5, acks 5/5
      forwarding latency .................... 0.76 ms (eth3 -> eth4, same frame)
      control, no service dhcp-relay ........ 0 relayed, offers 0/5
      control, no server address ............ 0 relayed, offers 0/5
      hops=2 (below threshold) .............. relayed, arrives at the server with hops=3
      hops=10 (at threshold) ................ dropped, 0 relayed, offers 0/5
CAVEAT:  The hop-count threshold was exercised only at its default of 10; `ip dhcp-relay
         maxhops` was never set to another value, so a configured threshold is not
         covered. One relay hop and one configured server address only; IPv4 only. The
         relay's ARP for the server was pre-resolved with a static entry (see TOPOLOGY),
         so the first-DISCOVER-consumed-by-ARP behaviour is not part of the counts.

