    (VLAN 48 access)                         + tcpdump, counts what the DUT relayed

  DUT     : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2, S/N A2WQS700B, relay MAC e01a.ead4.7043,
            standalone Active Master, sin_x96056-20261012-24
  client  : tb277 eth3 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e -> swi_d port1.0.10  (1000BASE-T, untagged VLAN 10)
  server  : tb277 eth4 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f -> swi_d port1.0.48  (1000BASE-T, untagged VLAN 48)
  SVIs    : vlan10 192.168.10.1/24 (client side), vlan48 192.168.48.1/24 (server side)
  static  : arp 192.168.48.2 000d.b955.770f port1.0.48 -- pre-resolves the relay's ARP for
            the scapy server, so no measured DISCOVER is consumed triggering it
  tools   : tools/dhcp4.py (client and server, scapy) on tb277;
            tcpdump on BOTH eth3 and eth4 for every leg, so each leg counts what was sent
            and what was relayed independently of the tool's own tally;
            tools/cfg.py and tools/ckcon.py drive the DUT console; tools/rc2cfg.py saved
            swi_d.cfg.
            Client, every leg:
              dhcp4.py client eth3 --mac <base> --clients 5 --gap 1 --broadcast
                       --prl 1,3,6,51 --wait 3
            Server, every leg:
              dhcp4.py server eth4 --server-ip 192.168.48.2 --pool-start 192.168.10.100
                       --pool-end 192.168.10.110 --mask 255.255.255.0
                       --router 192.168.10.1 --lease 3600 --echo-option82

  Method: a ping cannot show a relay rewriting giaddr, so every leg sends crafted
  DHCPDISCOVERs with a distinct chaddr and xid per client (BOOTP broadcast flag set) and
  is counted three independent ways: the eth3 capture (what went on the wire), the eth4
  capture (what the DUT relayed) and the scapy server's own per-frame record (giaddr,
  hops, source, chaddr). Every positive leg is paired with a control in the same
  configuration that must produce zero on eth4.

