  => STEP 1 PASS: every client frame was relayed, with giaddr rewritten from 0.0.0.0 to
     the client-side SVI 192.168.10.1 (which is what lets the server pick the client's
     subnet), hops incremented 0 -> 1, sourced from the server-side SVI and unicast to
     the configured server address. Each client's chaddr was preserved and each received
     its own distinct lease, and every OFFER and ACK was delivered back to the right
     client. Nothing here could be seen unless the relay were working.

