  => STEP 4 PASS: a request two hops out is relayed and its hop count incremented to 3; a
     request already at the threshold of 10 is dropped and never reaches the server. The
     threshold is therefore enforced, at the default the CLI reference documents, and the
     pair rules out any other cause -- the two legs differ in one byte of the request.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REMOVAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Removal was exercised by the two controls, which are the no-forms themselves:
  `no service dhcp-relay`                        -> relaying stops entirely (STEP 2)
  `no ip dhcp-relay server-address 192.168.48.2` -> `show ip dhcp-relay` reports
                                                    "List of servers :   no servers
                                                    configured" (STEP 3)
Both were re-applied afterwards and STEP 4 measured full relay function again, so neither
no-form left residue that blocked the feature from being restored.
